{"schema":2,"commit":"091d26d6d6b922a0a8979e3f88bdfb43f620821e","branch":"feat/window-close-and-ota","base_sha":"322ebcc4c0e7e8c34070900d14d129258dccffa9","message":"fix: install OTA updates through PackageInstaller\n\nThe refresh button found 2.2.3, downloaded it, and reported\n\"Kurulum reddedildi (imza uyuşmuyor?)\" for a build signed with exactly the same\nplatform certificate as the one already running. The signature was never the\nproblem.\n\ninstall() shelled out to `pm install -r` with a path inside the app's private\ncache. pm does not read the file — it hands the path to the package manager\nservice, which opens it from its own process and SELinux context, where that\ndirectory is not readable. The install failed for a reason nobody could see:\ninstall() returned a bare boolean, and UpdateHook mapped every false to the one\nmessage it had. The pm output that would have named the real error was captured\ninto a StringBuilder and discarded.\n\nA PackageInstaller session takes no path. We open the archive ourselves, as the\napp, and stream it into the session, so no second process ever has to reach our\ncache. Approach taken from merthankaraman/DriveHub_Dort, which hit the same wall\non the same head unit.\n\nConsequences worth knowing when reading a future failure:\n\n- Committing a session is asynchronous, so the refresh button can only say an\n  install started. OtaInstallResultReceiver has the verdict, and surfaces the\n  package manager's own INSTALL_FAILED_* text rather than guessing.\n- STATUS_PENDING_USER_ACTION is not an error. The receiver launches the\n  confirmation activity the platform supplies.\n- The PendingIntent must be MUTABLE or it arrives with no status extras.\n\ninstall() now returns an enum, so a certificate mismatch, an unparseable or\nwrong-package archive, and a failed session each say what they are.\n\nAlso checks the archive's package name against ours, which was a genuine gap:\nthe platform key signs every app on this unit, so a certificate match alone\nnever meant the APK was this app.\n\nThe `pm install -r` exit-code test goes with the shell-out it covered. Nothing\nin the session path is exercisable off-device.\n\nREQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES and the receiver are declared in the unstable manifest\nonly — the stable channel has no updater at all, and its merged manifest was\nchecked to confirm it gains neither.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","coding_time_nanos":23909974000,"totals":{"added_lines":249,"ai_added_lines":249,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":34,"ai_deleted_lines":0,"human_deleted_lines":34,"files":7,"tokens":{"input":7,"output":5222,"cache_read":2481850,"cache_write":8883},"models":{"claude-opus-5":249}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":249,"suggested_lines":890,"accepted_lines":249,"tokens":{"input":7,"output":5222,"cache_read":2481850,"cache_write":8883}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":0,"cli":249,"completion":0,"human":34},"files":[{"path":"OTA.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":33,"deleted_lines":7,"ai_added_lines":33,"human_deleted_lines":7,"lines":[{"start":89,"end":89,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":89,"end":89,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":90,"end":92,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":92,"end":92,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":93,"end":93,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":94,"end":95,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":96,"end":96,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":96,"end":97,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":98,"end":98,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":98,"end":98,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":99,"end":124,"type":"add","author_ty